+Unseen-task first-send enrichment is a full CURRENT row. Keep its current status with the current status's persisted capture descriptor (including a status equality check); never splice an old delta status into new metadata and never use merely the latest event at send. Seen-task deltas retain their own captured association. Already frozen uncertain snapshots are unchanged even after newer local edits. Explicit definitive schema/transient refusal may produce a new identity through existing bounded remap; carry status_origin into each replacement INSERT. Permanent synthetic-parent refusals neither create diagnostic fanout nor poison later synthesis with a cached refusal. A materialized retry in backoff suppresses competing parent synthesis. Existing pending task envelopes are selected before their unacknowledged dependents, even when their durable FIFO timestamp is later or outside the original batch. Backoff/quarantine holds dependents without consuming their attempt budget, but selection scans onward for unrelated work before applying the batch limit. The pre-feed-head filter is reapplied as a dependency constraint: it must not leave a child eligible when it removed that child's promoted parent.
 
 ## Evidenced why-chain
 
@@ -27,6 +27,16 @@ Broad CI of native head4de59d3a then caught shared-transaction integration regre
 
 The next broad run at0dc03e exposed the same family at a different entry: standalone `SYNC_SCHEMA_SQL` consumers intentionally have no `tasks` table, so the identity-cleanup CREATE TRIGGER failed at schema boot. Three unchanged drain consumer files reproduced RED, and a fresh/repeated standalone-schema regression failed before repair. The task-specific trigger now lives in `wanted_triggers`, where application tables exist; FK cleanup and identity revocation remain unchanged. Six-file validation including all three drain consumers, origin capture/repairs and native identity replacement passes51 tests (`core-schema-green2.log`). This extends integration coverage rather than modifying the drain fixtures to hide the dependency.
 
+## Parent retry regression (review6005624020)
+
+Problem: on unchanged66bf8e, one synthetic-parent storage refusal leaves its task/comment/event rejected after20 attempts even after the Board is healthy. The reviewer's unchanged probes reproduce4 failures/8 passes: both capability modes fail permanent-delivery and beyond-batch parent-order controls (`parent-review-red.log`).
+
+Why1: a child reaches the Board before its unacknowledged parent, poisoning that card's remaining request ops through `depends_on_rejected`.
+Why2: a refused synthetic parent is materialized at the FIFO tail, but a global pending-parent check prevents any new synthesis; both retries then share backoff and retain child-before-parent order.
+Root(happened): suppressing duplicate producers did not enforce the corresponding materialized-parent dependency. Root(not caught): earlier hubs accepted a parent after rejecting its child, unlike real Board request-order semantics. Recurrence: this corrects the earlier bounded-row-growth countermeasure; it does not revert its one-parent ownership rule.
+
+Countermeasures/proof: select the oldest existing pending parent before dependents without mutating identity, timestamps or frozen bytes; defer children while parent is in backoff/held; scan past that prefix before limiting; retain pre-feed-head dependency filtering. Unchanged reviewer probes now pass12/12, including peak-one-parent inventory and cached permanent-refusal recovery (`parent-review-green.log`). Additional three dependency selection controls and containment rekey test pass (`parent-final2-green.log`). The containment test freezes a seen-row request, strips lifecycle fields with a new identity, and proves next-send stored/wire identity matches the replacement, never old frozen bytes. That is not proof for every unacknowledged full-snapshot/containment combination. Explicitly rejected ops may remap because the server caches their definitive refusal; no-charge byte-preservation applies to uncertain sends, not explicit rejects.
+
 ## Coverage boundaries
 
 - Pre-upgrade or unbound historical uncertain sends cannot recover their original envelope or origin. Legacy ambiguity after reopen remains documented; never claim universal old-client safety.
